/* book exam traps: Temperature is not heat or internal energy. Equal readings mean no net heat flow on contact, not equal energies. | The offset is 273.15 for °C to K, but the triple point of water is 273.16 K (0.01 °C). Do not swap them in the gas-thermometer formula. | Two thermometers calibrated at the same fixed points agree only at those points. Between them they can differ, as the thermocouple reads 58.33 °C at a true 50 °C. | A thermometer shows its own temperature. Read it only after it stops changing, when it is in equilibrium with the body. | A temperature difference of 10 °C is 10 K, not 283.15 K. */
